            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Islandartist"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is a classic that my mom made regularly when I was young. I made it exactly as written with the small addition of 1tsp of cinnamon and 1/2tsp of cloves which is what my mother used to add and I threw the chocolate chips on top of the cake just before I put it in the oven. Love this recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-31T19:05:50.067Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Roni"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a good starter recipe. I made it gluten free. I used cup to cup gf flour, vanilla Greek yogurt, 1 c sugar, 1 c chocolate chunks, omitted the vinegar, milk and oil and I drained the zucchini by squeezing the liquid out. Everything else the same. Baked at 325° for 35 minutes. Moist, not too sweet. Yummy!",
            "datePublished": "2023-09-15T17:12:33.023Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was delicious! It was moist and fluffy and had very good flavor. I used my fresh garden grown zucchini! I added some chocolate chips in the mix also, along with some walnuts and coconut flakes. I'll be making this again!",
            "datePublished": "2021-08-28T00:44:40.580Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Krin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love this recipe! I make it with a gluten free flour blend and it is perfect and decadent.",
            "datePublished": "2024-06-06T14:21:57.354Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TribePride"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Really good. I did increase the cocoa powder by 50%, used far less chocolate chips (a full cup was way too much for me, and next time I might use mini chocolate chips instead) and replaced both the oil and butter with unsweetened applesauce, and it turned out delicious and moist! Very satisfying for chocoholic health nuts like me. :) And a great way to sneak in a little extra veggie intake! I'm not sure why one reviewer squeezed the moisture out of his/her zucchini, because generally when you bake with zucchini the idea is that the vegetable provides some necessary moisture to the finished product so you DON'T want to press it...but I guess it depends on your moisture preference. I would recommend not squeezing your zucchini though, whether you're making this recipe or brownies or zucchini bread, but then again I love moist cakes/brownies/breads!",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-22T19:30:18.117Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ginny"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was moist and yummy. I added a topping of toasted pecans and drizzled homemade caramel over it. I think I also added pecans to the cake batter. I didn't get to taste the finish product because it sold out at the church bake sale.",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-22T14:14:05.560Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "C Waite"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a very dense, moist, and delicious chocolate cake. This will be our go to recipe during zucchini season and beyond. Along with the semi-sweet choc. chips-3/4 cup, I had also added a 1/2 cup of white chocolate chips, and used applesauce in place of the oil. Wow! So good. This cake is good without frosting, with frosting, and my favorite, heated up then topped off with choc. chip ice cream. Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2015-07-20T10:59:38.207Z"
          },
          {
